From: FearLauncher
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: default-disable AFBC on Android

AFBC compressed textures frequently corrupt Minecraft block/chunk
textures on Mali GPUs (G52/G57/G610/G615) when used through kbase +
OSMesa. UI and sky can look fine while world blocks glitch.

Default-enable PAN_DBG_NO_AFBC on Android builds. Users can still
override via PAN_MESA_DEBUG if needed.

---
src/gallium/drivers/panfrost/pan_screen.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

Apply with:
  patch -p1 < patches/0001-android-default-noafbc.patch

or manually insert after debug_get_flags_option("PAN_MESA_DEBUG"...):

#if defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(ANDROID)
   if (!(dev->debug & PAN_DBG_NO_AFBC))
      dev->debug |= PAN_DBG_NO_AFBC;
#endif

Exact context in pan_screen.c around device screen create:

   dev->debug =
      debug_get_flags_option("PAN_MESA_DEBUG", panfrost_debug_options, 0);
   /* INSERT ANDROID NOAFBC BLOCK HERE */
   screen->max_afbc_packing_ratio = debug_get_num_option(
      "PAN_MAX_AFBC_PACKING_RATIO", DEFAULT_MAX_AFBC_PACKING_RATIO);
